window.GM_SEARCH_INDEX = [{"u": "about.html", "t": "Who We Are", "d": "GrubMarket is the largest private food technology company in the U.S., connecting growers, distributors, businesses, and homes across the food supply chain.", "b": "Home › Company › Who We Are Who we are A food technology company on a mission to digitally transform the American food supply chain. Founded in 2014, GrubMarket is the largest private food technology company in the U.S. We operate across the U.S. and Canadian food supply chain — serving business customers and end consumers, and providing software-as-a-service that digitally transforms businesses at every step from farm to table. Today the company does business across all 50 U.S. states and in nine countries internationally, with commerce touching more than 70 countries worldwide. What we do We connect growers, distributors, businesses, and homes through three tightly integrated offerings. Our B2B marketplace lets grocers, restaurants, schools, and government buyers source thousands of products at exclusive wholesale prices. Our AI-powered software platform — anchored by WholesaleWare, the food industry's fastest-growing cloud ERP — runs inventory, warehouse operations, grower accounting, and general ledger for wholesalers and distributors, while GrubAssist (the industry's first virtual AI assistant), AI Orders, Orders IO, and GrubPay automate ordering, payments, and business insight. And our farm-fresh delivery network, through local hubs like Good Eggs, SPUD, and FreshGOGO, brings groceries to homes and offices for up to 50% less than retail. How we grow GrubMarket has grown to more than 70 acquisitions by combining strategic buys with organic expansion of its software and m"}, {"u": "accessibility.html", "t": "Accessibility Statement", "d": "GrubMarket's commitment to accessible digital experiences for all users across our marketplace and software platforms.", "b": "Home › Accessibility Accessibility Statement Last updated June 2026 Placeholder text for this redesign prototype. Replace with GrubMarket's official accessibility statement before launch. Our commitment GrubMarket is committed to making its websites, marketplace, and software accessible to everyone, including people with disabilities. We want every customer to be able to source, sell, and order food with ease. Standards we follow We aim to conform to the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 Level AA and to align with applicable requirements such as the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). What we do Support keyboard navigation and visible focus across interactive elements. Menus open with Enter, Space or Arrow Down, close with Escape, and expose their state through aria-expanded . Use semantic markup and ARIA labels so assistive technologies can interpret content. Maintain color contrast at WCAG AA (4.5:1 for body text, 3:1 for focus indicators) and scalable, legible typography. Provide text alternatives for meaningful images. Respect the operating system's reduced-motion setting. Known limitations We test this site continuously and publish what we have not yet resolved: Mobile touch-target sizes have not been audited against the 44 × 44 px minimum. The site has not been tested end to end with a screen reader; our checks so far have been automated plus manual keyboard testing. The contact form currently falls back to email if submission fails. Ongoing effort Acce"}, {"u": "article-monitoring-ai.html", "t": "Monitoring AI Agent flags critical issues", "d": "How GrubMarket's Monitoring AI Agent automatically detects and alerts distributors to critical business issues in real time.", "b": "Home › In the News › Enterprise AI GrubMarket announces Monitoring AI Agent to detect and alert on critical business issues A new GrubAssist AI agent that continuously monitors key business data, detects anomalies, and sends proactive alerts — shifting teams from reactive firefighting to proactive control. Enterprise AI · January 27, 2026 Food supply chain operators face pressure to move quickly, remain efficient, and navigate constant change while managing perishability, complex logistics, and shifting customer demand. GrubMarket has released a new specialized AI agent — the Monitoring AI Agent — within GrubAssist AI. It provides continuous, passive monitoring of key business and operational data, automatically detecting anomalies, identifying market condition changes, and surfacing shifts in critical performance metrics. It sends proactive alerts based on custom trigger conditions, enabling teams to identify issues sooner and respond more rapidly. From reactive firefighting to proactive control Many food businesses operate reactively: problems surface after they occur, reporting happens manually, and time is scarce. Although data exists across ERP, eCommerce, payments, and finance systems, most teams lack the bandwidth for continuous analysis. The Monitoring AI Agent shifts businesses from reactive to proactive operations, with configurable alerts for scenarios such as: A key customer has gone more than 7 days without placing an order A vendor shortage is projected to impac"}, {"u": "article-sales-ai-agent.html", "t": "Sales AI Agent for prospecting and quotes", "d": "How GrubMarket's Sales AI Agent transforms prospecting and quote creation for food distributors and wholesalers.", "b": "Home › In the News › Enterprise AI GrubMarket announces Sales AI Agent to transform prospecting and quote creation A new AI agent helps wholesale food distribution sales teams find prospects, analyze menus, build price sheets, and send proposals — in a single workflow. Enterprise AI · June 8, 2026 GrubMarket has announced the launch of Sales AI Agent, the newest specialized AI solution within the GrubMarket AI platform. Designed specifically for wholesale food distribution sales teams, Sales AI Agent helps users identify prospective customers, analyze menus and order guides, generate professional price sheets, and deliver proposals through a single AI-powered workflow. By combining prospect discovery, menu analysis, automated quote creation, and proposal delivery, Sales AI Agent helps distributors scale prospecting efforts, respond faster to opportunities, and compete more effectively in today's increasingly competitive market. Key capabilities Territory-based prospect discovery. Search by ZIP code or explore an interactive map to identify restaurants, foodservice operators, and retailers within target markets, with detailed business profiles to build targeted campaigns. AI-powered menu analysis. Upload photos or PDFs of menus and order guides, and the agent intelligently identifies products and recommends matching catalog items. Automated price sheet generation. Create professional, customer-ready price sheets using configured price groups or custom pricing — cutting the tim"}, {"u": "article-schoenmann.html", "t": "Acquiring Schoenmann Produce", "d": "GrubMarket acquires Schoenmann Produce, a Houston-based Gulf Coast distributor serving the region for over a century.", "b": "Home › In the News › Acquisition GrubMarket acquires Schoenmann Produce, a century-old Gulf Coast distributor The acquisition of a respected Houston-based distributor — serving the Gulf Coast for over 100 years — strengthens GrubMarket's presence across Texas and the broader region. Acquisition · April 15, 2026 We are thrilled to announce that GrubMarket has completed the acquisition of Schoenmann Produce, a highly respected Houston-based distributor that has been serving the Gulf Coast region for over 100 years. This partnership strengthens our presence in Texas and the broader Gulf Coast region as we continue to drive forward our mission to modernize the food supply chain through technology and innovation. Over a century of excellence Schoenmann Produce has built a strong reputation for quality, service, and reliability, supported by impressive infrastructure and long-standing customer and partner relationships established since the company's founding in 1910. Its capabilities include: A state-of-the-art 90,000 sq ft facility on 34.5 acres near Houston's Hobby Airport 75,000 sq ft of cold storage, a fully refrigerated dock, and advanced ripening rooms A Primus score of 100 — best-in-class food safety, traceability, and quality control Deep relationships across foodservice, retail, wholesale, healthcare, education, and maritime sectors A strong commitment to Texas-grown produce and local agriculture Joining GrubMarket reflects an important moment in the continued evolution o"}, {"u": "article-series-h.html", "t": "$50M Series H to fuel eCommerce and AI", "d": "GrubMarket raises a $50M Series H round at a $4.5B valuation to accelerate eCommerce and AI across the food supply chain.", "b": "Home › In the News › Funding GrubMarket raises $50M Series H to fuel eCommerce and AI transformation A $50 million round at a $4.5 billion pre-money valuation will accelerate GrubMarket's AI software and global eCommerce growth across the food supply chain. Funding · February 2, 2026 GrubMarket, an AI-powered technology company transforming the American food supply chain, announced a $50 million Series H financing round from Future Food Fund, Portfolia Funds, Liberty Street Funds, RD Heritage Group, Flume Ventures, MY Securities, and other participants, valuing the company at $4.5 billion pre-money. A round built on a year of major milestones The investment follows significant company achievements. GrubMarket acquired Delta Fresh Produce in April 2025, followed by its largest acquisition — Coast Citrus — in June 2025. The company launched its first-ever Inventory Management AI Agent in July 2025 to automate inventory workflows, and released a Reporting AI Agent in September 2025 for automated business analysis. GrubMarket also acquired Procurant, a SaaS trading platform facilitating $5.5 billion in annual Gross Merchandise Volume for over 850 customers across 14 countries. Investing from a position of strength GrubMarket has experienced an incredible acceleration in growth over the last 12 months. This Series H funding will turbocharge our AI software and business growth. Mike Xu, CEO of GrubMarket GrubMarket operates across all 50 U.S. states and has a global presence in nin"}, {"u": "article-spring-2026.html", "t": "Spring 2026 software release", "d": "Inside GrubMarket's Spring 2026 release, with new capabilities across WholesaleWare, Orders IO, and AI Orders.", "b": "Home › In the News › Software GrubMarket announces the Spring 2026 release of its AI-powered software ecosystem Significant new capabilities across WholesaleWare, Orders IO, and AI Orders — the industry's only fully integrated platform spanning ERP, AI, and eCommerce. Software · May 12, 2026 GrubMarket has announced the Spring 2026 product release for its software suite, introducing significant enhancements across WholesaleWare, Orders IO, and AI Orders. As the industry's only fully integrated technology platform spanning ERP, AI, and eCommerce, the Spring 2026 Release delivers new capabilities designed to help restaurant and foodservice distributors and produce wholesalers improve efficiency, elevate customer service, and drive profitability. WholesaleWare enhancements Automated work orders. Streamlines repacking and processing through automated creation and management of work orders, with real-time inventory and cost updates. New price groups. Flexible, rule-based pricing segmentation with item- and category-level overrides. Automated FIFO lot allocation. Optionally allocate lots automatically at shipment, in addition to pre-allocating and scanning to pick. Expanded EDI integrations. New integrations with Produce Alliance and Restaurant365 for seamless, automated order processing. New reports and platform enhancements. Purchasing guides, route summaries, charge insights, and improvements across sales orders, inventory, lot tracking, and accounting. AI Orders enhancements Mu"}, {"u": "article-time100.html", "t": "Named to the TIME100 Companies list", "d": "GrubMarket is named to the inaugural TIME100 Companies Industry Leaders list for transforming the food supply chain.", "b": "Home › In the News › Company GrubMarket named to the TIME100 Companies Industry Leaders list TIME recognizes GrubMarket among the companies making an extraordinary impact across their industries — reflecting our progress transforming the food supply chain through AI, eCommerce, and vertical SaaS. Company · April 29, 2026 We are pleased to share that GrubMarket has been named to the inaugural TIME100 Companies Industry Leaders list, recognizing companies making an extraordinary impact across their respective industries. This recognition reflects our continued progress in transforming the food supply chain through AI, eCommerce, and vertical SaaS solutions, as well as the strong momentum we've built over the past year. Recognition by TIME According to TIME's 2026 Most Influential Companies coverage, GrubMarket has established itself as both a leading technology provider and a major operator within the food supply chain. The company has scaled rapidly by combining strategic acquisitions with its AI-powered WholesaleWare platform, enabling food wholesalers and distributors to modernize their operations through automation, data-driven decision making, and digital infrastructure. TIME evaluated companies based on impact, innovation, ambition, and success, highlighting GrubMarket's unique position at the intersection of technology and the global food ecosystem. A year of growth and innovation This recognition follows a year of significant expansion and technological advancement. Key"}, {"u": "article.html", "t": "How AI is reshaping food distribution", "d": "How artificial intelligence is reshaping food distribution, from ordering and inventory to payments and logistics.", "b": "Home › In the News › Technology How AI is reshaping food distribution Automated order extraction is quietly removing hours of manual work from wholesalers' days — and changing what the supply chain can do. Sample article for this redesign prototype — replace with real editorial content before launch. For decades, the food supply chain has run on phone calls, faxes, and email threads. Orders arrive in a dozen formats, get re-keyed by hand, and errors compound at every step. GrubMarket's Enterprise AI was built to change that. From inbox to order, automatically Automated order extraction reads emails, texts, PDFs, and even voicemails, then turns them into clean, structured orders — no manual entry required. What used to take a sales team hours now happens in seconds. Why it matters for wholesalers Fewer errors mean fewer credits, happier customers, and time given back to teams who would rather be building relationships than typing line items. It also creates a clean data trail that powers better forecasting and pricing. Built for food, not generic Generic automation tools don't understand produce, perishability, or procurement. GrubMarket's models are trained on the realities of the food supply chain, so they handle the messy, real-world inputs the industry actually runs on. Back to all articles See Enterprise AI in action Find out how automated order extraction reduces cost and error across your operation. Explore Enterprise AI Book a demo"}, {"u": "blog.html", "t": "In the News", "d": "News, product releases, and insights from GrubMarket on AI, eCommerce, and the future of the food supply chain.", "b": "Home › News › In the News In the News Stories from across the food supply chain — technology, sustainability, and the people moving food forward. Press & updates Latest stories Acquisition Acquiring SPUD, a leading Canadian online grocery company The Vancouver-based grocer, founded in 1997, extends GrubMarket's home delivery into British Columbia and Alberta. July 21, 2026 Enterprise AI Sales AI Agent transforms prospecting and quote creation A new AI agent that automates prospecting and quote generation for food distributors. June 8, 2026 Software Spring 2026 release of our AI-powered software ecosystem Expanded AI capabilities roll out across the GrubMarket software platform. May 12, 2026 Company Named to the TIME100 Companies Industry Leaders list TIME recognizes GrubMarket as a leader transforming the food supply chain. April 29, 2026 Acquisition Acquiring Schoenmann Produce, a century-old Gulf Coast distributor Expanding GrubMarket's reach with a prominent Houston-based produce distributor. April 15, 2026 Funding Raising a $50M Series H to fuel eCommerce & AI New funding to accelerate the digital transformation of the food supply chain. February 2, 2026 Enterprise AI Monitoring AI Agent flags critical business issues automatically Proactive AI that detects operational problems and alerts teams in real time. January 27, 2026 View all news on the GrubMarket blog → Want updates in your inbox? Follow along as we share what's next for the food supply chain. Get in touch"}, {"u": "careers.html", "t": "Careers", "d": "Join GrubMarket. Open roles in engineering, AI, operations, and sales, building the technology behind the food supply chain.", "b": "Home › Company › Careers Build the future of food technology Join the team digitally transforming the American food supply chain — across engineering, AI, operations, and sales. View open roles Life at GrubMarket Where food meets technology What you'd actually be building Engineers here shipped the Sales AI Agent, the Monitoring AI Agent, and the Spring 2026 software release across WholesaleWare, Orders IO, and AI Orders — real products used daily by distributors moving perishable inventory, not internal tools or slide-deck features. GrubMarket has grown past 70 acquisitions and a $2.4B revenue run-rate while staying profitable, which means teams ship fast but inherit real operational constraints: warehouses that can't go down, payments that have to reconcile exactly, and customers who will notice immediately if an order guide is wrong. Open roles Where you fit in Full Stack Software Engineer Engineering · San Francisco, CA Apply Senior Software Sales Account Executive Sales · San Francisco, CA Apply Digital Marketing Manager Marketing · San Francisco, CA Apply Marketing Specialist Marketing · San Francisco, CA Apply Online Grocery Packers — Morning Shift Operations · San Francisco, CA Apply Online Grocery Packers — Night Shift Operations · San Francisco, CA Apply Roles shown are GrubMarket's current openings. The official openings page is always authoritative — check there for the latest list. Don't see your role? We're always looking for talented people who care about food "}, {"u": "catalog.html", "t": "Product Catalog", "d": "Browse GrubMarket's wholesale product catalog: fresh produce, proteins, dairy, pantry staples, floral, and specialty organic items.", "b": "Home › Buy & Sell › Product Catalog Product catalog Thousands of quality products across the U.S. and Canada, sourced from a nationwide grower and distributor network. Buy wholesale What you can source Everything a food business needs, in one place Browse by category and order at exclusive wholesale prices, with delivery on your schedule. Fresh produce Seasonal fruits and vegetables, conventional and organic, from growers nationwide. See examples Tomatoes, peppers & leafy greens Citrus & stone fruit Berries & melons Root vegetables & alliums Herbs Proteins & seafood Meat, poultry, and seafood sourced for quality and consistency. See examples Chicken & poultry Beef & pork Fresh & frozen seafood Shellfish Deli & prepared meats Dairy & eggs Everyday staples to round out your order in a single delivery. See examples Milk & cream Cheese Butter & yogurt Eggs Plant-based alternatives Pantry & dry goods Shelf-stable essentials for restaurants, grocers, and foodservice. See examples Rice, grains & flour Oils & vinegars Canned & jarred goods Spices & seasonings Sauces & condiments Specialty & organic Hard-to-find and certified-organic items for differentiated menus and shelves. See examples Certified-organic produce Gluten-free & allergen-friendly Plant-based proteins International & ethnic ingredients Artisanal & small-batch goods Floral Fresh-cut flowers and arrangements for retail and events. See examples Cut flowers & bouquets Greenery & foliage Potted plants Event & wedding arrang"}, {"u": "community.html", "t": "Community Hub", "d": "Join the GrubMarket community to share feedback, connect with grocers, growers, and distributors, and help shape the platform.", "b": "Home › News › Community Hub Community hub Connect with the network of buyers, growers, and distributors moving food forward. Get involved More than a marketplace The GrubMarket community is where the people who run the food supply chain share what works, learn from each other, and help shape what we build next. Share feedback Tell us what's working and what isn't — your input drives the product roadmap. Product council Join customers who help prioritize and test new features before release. Connect & learn Meet other buyers, growers, and distributors and trade practical know-how. Community programs are being expanded for this redesign — reach out to get early access. Community, not just customer support GrubMarket's origins as a network of local CSA farms and food hubs — going back to the Farmigo platform, which connected hundreds of small farms to more than 3,000 buyer communities — mean the company has always depended on real relationships between growers, distributors, and the people who buy from them, not just software. The Community Hub is a continuation of that: a place to trade practical advice with other operators who've solved the same warehouse or pricing problem, not a support ticket queue. Join the community Get involved, share your story, and help move food forward. Get involved Customer stories"}, {"u": "contact.html", "t": "Contact", "d": "Contact GrubMarket. Tell us whether you're a grocer, grower, distributor, investor, or press, and we'll route you to the right team.", "b": "Home › Contact Let's talk Tell us a little about you and what you're looking for — wholesale buying, selling your harvest, software, or delivery — and the right team will get back to you. Name Email Company or farm (optional) I'm a… Grocer or restaurant Grower or farmer Distributor or wholesaler Enterprise / software buyer Investor Household or office Something else How can we help? (optional) Send message"}, {"u": "cookie-policy.html", "t": "Cookie Policy", "d": "Learn how GrubMarket uses cookies and similar technologies across its websites and services.", "b": "Home › Cookie Policy Cookie Policy Last updated June 2026 Placeholder text for this redesign prototype. Replace with GrubMarket's official cookie policy before launch. 1. What cookies are Cookies are small text files placed on your device to help websites function, remember your preferences, and understand how the site is used. 2. How we use cookies Essential — required for the site and marketplace to work, including sign-in and checkout. Preferences — remember choices such as your region or language. Analytics — help us understand traffic and improve the experience. Marketing — measure and tailor the relevance of our communications. 3. Managing your choices You can accept or reject non-essential cookies through our consent banner, and control cookies at any time through your browser settings. Blocking some cookies may affect how parts of the site work. 4. Third-party cookies Some cookies are set by third-party services we use for analytics and payments. Their use of data is governed by their own privacy policies. 5. Changes to this policy We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by the \"last updated\" date above. 6. Contact Questions about our use of cookies? Reach out through our contact page . See also our Privacy Policy ."}, {"u": "corporate-governance.html", "t": "Corporate Governance", "d": "GrubMarket's corporate governance: the board, committees, and policies guiding the company's growth and accountability.", "b": "Home › Investor Relations › Corporate Governance Corporate governance How GrubMarket is governed — our board, committees, and the policies that guide responsible operation. Preview Governance framework shown for this redesign. Full charters and policies will be published here; board and committee composition would be formalized ahead of any public offering. Board & committees Oversight structure Board of Directors Provides strategic oversight and represents the long-term interests of shareholders and stakeholders. Audit Committee Oversees financial reporting, internal controls, and the independent auditor. Compensation Committee Reviews executive compensation and incentive alignment with performance. Nominating & Governance Committee Oversees board composition, succession, and governance practices. Policies & documents Governance documents Our governing policies will be available for download here. Corporate Governance Guidelines Board roles, independence, and operating principles. PDF · Coming soon Code of Business Conduct & Ethics Standards of conduct for directors, officers, and employees. PDF · Coming soon Committee Charters Audit, Compensation, and Nominating & Governance charters. PDF · Coming soon Whistleblower & Insider Trading Policies Reporting protections and trading compliance. PDF · Coming soon Learn more Explore our leadership, filings, and investor materials. Leadership team SEC filings"}, {"u": "customers.html", "t": "Customer Stories", "d": "Real stories from GrubMarket partners like Coast Citrus Distributors and Schoenmann Produce on scaling with our platform.", "b": "Home › News › Customers Customer stories How growers, distributors, and businesses grow with GrubMarket's marketplace, software, and AI. Our ability to offer superior services and the finest quality produce year after year is powered by our deep operational know-how, enduring relationships with our customers and vendors, and our investments in world-class digital transformation. Carole Shandler President of Shapiro-Gilman-Shandler, GrubMarket Stories Growing with GrubMarket Distribution Scaling a regional distributor A Gulf Coast distributor modernizes ordering and traceability on WholesaleWare and Orders IO. Explore the software → Getting paid, on time Growers reach more buyers across North America and get paid reliably through the GrubMarket network. For growers → Fresh to the door Families and offices get farm-fresh food delivered through local food hubs. Get delivery → Illustrative stories representing the customers GrubMarket serves — named case studies to follow. Real partners, real transitions When Isabel Freeland, President & CEO of Coast Citrus Distributors, joined GrubMarket in its largest acquisition to date, she pointed to the company's \"ownership mentality\" culture and GrubMarket's investment in AI as reasons the fit made sense. Mark Steakley of Schoenmann Produce, a Houston distributor with over a century of history, described joining GrubMarket as \"an important moment in the continued evolution\" of a business his family had run for generations. Neither story is"}, {"u": "delivery.html", "t": "Home & Office Delivery", "d": "Farm-fresh groceries delivered to your home or office through GrubMarket's local hubs: Good Eggs, SPUD, FreshGOGO, and DO Organics.", "b": "Home › Buy & Sell › Home & Office Delivery Home & office delivery Farm-fresh food delivered to your door — at prices up to 50% less than grocery stores. How it works Fresh food, fewer middlemen GrubMarket delivers through a family of local food hubs. Order online and get farm-fresh groceries delivered to your home or office. 1 · Pick your hub Choose the local brand that serves your area to start ordering. 2 · Shop fresh Browse produce and groceries sourced directly from growers. 3 · Get it delivered Farm-fresh food arrives at your door or office on a schedule that works for you. Local food hubs Choose the brand that serves your area Each hub runs on its own ordering site. Pick yours to get started: Why it costs less than the grocery store Traditional grocery pricing carries the cost of a distributor, a wholesaler, and a retail markup before food ever reaches a shelf. GrubMarket's delivery hubs source directly from the same grower and distributor network that supplies the B2B marketplace, so a box of produce skips several of those markups on its way to your door — which is how prices land up to 50% below grocery store prices for comparable quality. It's also the same infrastructure GrubMarket built for wholesale: the trucks, the cold storage, and the grower relationships behind Good Eggs, SPUD, FreshGOGO, and DO Organics are the same ones behind pallets shipped to restaurants and grocers — home delivery is simply a second use of a supply chain GrubMarket already runs at scale."}, {"u": "distributors.html", "t": "Distributors & Wholesalers", "d": "Run inventory, warehouse, purchasing, and accounting on WholesaleWare, the food industry's fastest-growing ERP for distributors.", "b": "Home › Who We Serve › Distributors & Wholesalers For distributors & wholesalers Run your whole operation on one platform — ERP, eCommerce, payments, and AI, built for perishables. See the software One connected stack The tools to run and grow your business GrubMarket replaces disconnected, legacy tools with an integrated platform purpose-built for the fresh food supply chain. WholesaleWare ERP Inventory, warehouse, purchasing, lot tracking, and accounting in one system. Explore ERP → Orders IO Custom-branded mobile ordering that feeds straight into your ERP. See Orders IO → GrubPay Collect and reconcile payments without the manual AR work. See GrubPay → Enterprise AI AI agents that automate order entry, monitoring, and reporting. Explore AI → Why it matters Less manual work, fewer errors Automate order entry AI Orders turns emails, texts, and PDFs into clean, structured orders in seconds. Real-time inventory Know what you have and what it costs, updated as you buy and sell. Grow with the network Tap into GrubMarket's buyers and suppliers across North America. What acquired distributors gain by joining When Coast Citrus Distributors — a 1950-founded, 90-truck operation and GrubMarket's largest acquisition to date — and Schoenmann Produce, a Houston distributor with a perfect Primus food safety score, joined GrubMarket, neither had to abandon what already worked. Instead, each gained access to WholesaleWare, GrubAssist AI, AI Orders, Orders IO, and GrubPay on top of existing op"}, {"u": "enterprise-ai.html", "t": "Enterprise AI", "d": "GrubMarket's enterprise AI: GrubAssist and AI Orders automate ordering, insight, and operations across the food supply chain.", "b": "Home › Tech › Enterprise AI Enterprise AI for the food supply chain Innovative AI from GrubMarket empowers people and businesses across the supply chain with deep insights, intelligent analysis, voice-powered assistance, and automated order extraction across channels. Explore capabilities See the ERP suite Built for food, not generic AI that understands your business Generic tools don't know produce, perishability, or procurement. GrubMarket's Enterprise AI — GrubAssist™, AI Orders™, and generative pricing intelligence — is trained on the realities of the food supply chain, turning messy orders, calls, and data into clean, actionable operations. Automated order extraction across channels Voice-powered assistance for the floor Deep insights & intelligent analysis Talk to sales Capabilities From inbox to insight, automatically AI Orders™ Automatic order extraction from emails, texts, and voicemails — capturing orders 24/7, no manual entry. GrubAssist™ The first virtual AI assistant for the food supply chain — hands-free help with mobile and voice. GrubMarket AI Generative AI delivering real-time wholesale pricing and deep market insight to buyers and sellers. A growing family of AI agents Enterprise AI isn't one tool — it's a fast-expanding roster of specialized agents inside GrubAssist, each built for a specific job. The Sales AI Agent discovers prospects by territory, reads a restaurant's menu or order guide, and generates a customer-ready price sheet in minutes instead of ho"}, {"u": "events.html", "t": "Events & Trade Shows", "d": "Meet the GrubMarket team at earnings webcasts, investor summits, and trade shows across the food supply chain.", "b": "Home › News › Events Events & trade shows Where to meet the GrubMarket team — webcasts, industry conferences, and trade shows across the food supply chain. Upcoming events Join us Aug 06 Q2 2026 Earnings Webcast 5:00 PM ET · Online Details → Sep 18 Food & AgTech Investor Summit New York, NY · Management presenting Details → Nov 12 Annual Investor Day San Francisco, CA · In-person & webcast Details → Sample events for this redesign — dates, times, and registration links are placeholders. GrubMarket is privately held and does not currently hold public earnings webcasts. Replace with the real calendar before launch. Trade shows Meet us on the floor Beyond webcasts and investor events, GrubMarket exhibits and speaks at leading produce, foodservice, and food-technology shows across North America — with live demos of WholesaleWare, AI Orders, and Orders IO. See where we exhibit Why we show up in person GrubMarket's software serves an industry that still runs largely on relationships built face to face — produce buyers who've worked with the same growers for decades, distributors who trust a handshake more than a sales deck. Trade shows and investor events are where that trust gets built: a chance to demo AI Orders on an actual order guide, walk through WholesaleWare with a warehouse manager who's skeptical of \"another system,\" or explain to investors what a $50 million Series H at a $4.5 billion valuation actually funds. Want to connect? Reach out to schedule a meeting or request a"}, {"u": "find-a-wholesaler.html", "t": "Find a Wholesaler", "d": "Find a GrubMarket wholesaler by state. Search our nationwide network of regional produce distributors and partners.", "b": "Home › Buy & Sell › Find a Wholesaler Find a wholesaler Search by state to see where GrubMarket's network reaches — from acquired regional distributors to nationwide wholesale coverage. Coverage Search GrubMarket's network by state Named partner in this state Reachable through our nationwide network Select a state Where should we start? Search above, or choose any state from the list or the regions to see how GrubMarket serves that area. Only currently active GrubMarket companies are named below. States without a named partner are served through GrubMarket's nationwide wholesale network — contact us to source there. Not seeing your state's details yet? GrubMarket ships wholesale nationwide — tell us where you are and we'll get you sourcing. Buy Wholesale Talk to our team"}, {"u": "grocers.html", "t": "Grocers & Restaurants", "d": "Keep shelves and menus stocked through GrubMarket's B2B network: quality inventory at wholesale prices, delivered nationwide.", "b": "Home › Who We Serve › Grocers & Restaurants For grocers & restaurants Source quality products at exclusive, low prices — with reliable fulfillment you can plan around. Buy wholesale Why GrubMarket Keep shelves and kitchens stocked Whether you run a market or a menu, GrubMarket connects you to a nationwide network at prices the middle layers can't match. Exclusive pricing Buy direct from a nationwide grower and distributor network at low, wholesale prices. Consistent quality Dependable, high-quality products so your shelves and dishes stay reliable. Delivery on your schedule Fulfillment you can plan around, across the U.S. and Canada. One platform Order, reorder, and manage it all online or from the Orders IO app. Skip the layers between you and the grower A typical grocer or restaurant buys through a chain of intermediaries — grower, packer, regional wholesaler, broker — each adding a markup before the product reaches a receiving dock. GrubMarket's network compresses that chain: sourcing runs through the same grower and distributor relationships that supply the wholesale marketplace, including established regional players like Coast Citrus Distributors and Schoenmann Produce, so pricing reflects fewer hands touching the product. Ordering itself runs through the Orders IO app or the web catalog, both synced to real-time inventory on WholesaleWare — so what you see available is what actually ships, not a static price sheet that's already out of date. Source smarter Create an ac"}, {"u": "growers.html", "t": "For Growers & Farmers", "d": "Sell your harvest through GrubMarket. Reach a nationwide buyer network, manage CSA boxes, and get paid reliably.", "b": "Home › Who We Serve › Growers You grow it. We'll help you sell it — and get you paid. GrubMarket connects your farm to thousands of buyers across the U.S. and Canada, handles the logistics and the paperwork, and pays you fairly and on time. No cold calls, no middle-man headaches, no tech to wrestle with. Become a supplier See how it works Why growers choose us More buyers. Fair prices. On-time payments. Reach grocers, restaurants, and schools nationwide — without cold calls. Get paid fairly and on time — we handle settlements and statements for you. Sell straight to your community with CSA & food-hub tools. Keep doing what you do best — we take care of the logistics and the tech. Become a supplier What you get Everything you need to sell more, with less hassle A nationwide marketplace Your produce in front of thousands of vetted buyers across the U.S. and Canada — we bring the demand to you. Grower payments, simplified Settlements, statements, and on-time pay handled automatically — so you always know where you stand. Tools made for farms CSA management, online ordering, and mobile-friendly software that's simple enough to use from the field. Built on tools made for CSAs and small farms Much of GrubMarket's grower-facing technology traces back to Farmigo, a platform trusted by hundreds of CSA farms across 25 states, which has helped connect farms to more than 3,000 communities and moved over 30 million pounds of produce directly from growers to members since 2009. That same i"}, {"u": "grubos.html", "t": "Enterprise AI", "d": "Enterprise AI is the single front door to GrubMarket's software, with eight modules spanning the entire food supply chain under one login.", "b": "Home › Tech › Enterprise AI Every GrubMarket platform, one place. Enterprise AI is the single front door to GrubMarket's software — every product and capability, organized into eight modules under one login, one contract, and one data layer. Select any module to see what's inside. Explore Enterprise AI 1 Field Labor Scheduling, time tracking & payroll for crews. Pacific Farm Management 2 Food Safety HACCP, inspections & compliance at every step. WaudWare / PICS 3 Warehouse Receiving, put-away, pick & pack, live inventory. WholesaleWare® WMS 4 EDI Automated trading-partner data exchange. WholesaleWare® EDI Procurant 5 Transportation Freight matching, dispatch & carrier management. Uber Freight 6 Commerce eCommerce, mobile B2B ordering & direct-to-consumer. Nova Libra / CORAL Orders IO Farmigo 7 AI GrubAssist, AI Orders & analytics. GrubAssist / AI Orders QBIX Analytics 8 ERP & Financials Produce ERP, accounting & payments in one ledger. Fresh Software / Thyme Parsemony / Profitsense Frantoni Granite State Software GrubPay A decade of acquisitions, one front door Same software, same customers. One brand, one login, one AI layer across every product GrubMarket has built or acquired. Explore Enterprise AI See the AI layer"}, {"u": "grubpay.html", "t": "GrubPay", "d": "GrubPay lets food businesses accept ACH and credit card payments in one secure, simple workflow built for the supply chain.", "b": "Home › Tech › GrubPay GrubPay The payments rail built into GrubMarket's software — so you get paid faster and reconcile automatically. Talk to sales Payments Collect and reconcile without the busywork GrubPay is embedded across WholesaleWare and Orders IO, turning invoicing, collection, and reconciliation into one connected flow. Get paid faster Accept card and ACH payments directly against invoices, shortening the time from delivery to cash. Automatic reconciliation Payments match back to orders and invoices automatically, cutting manual AR work. One connected flow Ordering, invoicing, and payment live in the same platform — no bolted-on tools. Secure by design Payment data is handled to industry security standards across every transaction. Product capabilities summarized for this redesign — contact us for current specifications. Why payments live inside the platform Most distributors collect payment through a system that doesn't talk to the one that generated the invoice — so someone spends hours a week matching bank deposits back to open orders by hand. Because GrubPay is embedded in WholesaleWare and Orders IO rather than bolted on, a payment automatically closes the invoice it belongs to the moment it clears, whether a customer paid through the mobile app, over the phone, or by ACH. That single change — payments and orders sharing one data layer — is what shortens the gap between delivery and cash, and it's the same principle behind everything else in the GrubMarket plat"}, {"u": "index.html", "t": "GrubMarket", "d": "GrubMarket connects growers, businesses, and homes across the U.S. and Canada, from wholesale buying to AI-powered software and farm-fresh delivery.", "b": "Built for grocers We're on a mission to digitally transform the American food supply chain industry. Founded in 2014, GrubMarket connects growers, businesses, and homes across the U.S. and Canada — from wholesale buying to AI-powered software and farm-fresh delivery. Buy Wholesale Sell your harvest → Find your GrubMarket Whether you grow, distribute, sell, or source, there's a place for you at GrubMarket Grocers & restaurants Source quality products at exclusive, low prices. Buy wholesale → Growers & farmers Reach more buyers and get paid, on time. Sell your harvest → Distributors & wholesalers Run your whole operation on one platform. Explore the software → Home & office Farm-fresh food delivered to your door. Get delivery → An industry leader The largest private food technology company in the U.S. $2.4B Annual revenue 70+ Companies acquired 10,000+ Business customers $4.5B Valuation Profitable · 3 years running CNBC Disruptor 50 · 2023–2025 TIME100 Industry Leaders · 2026 Backed by Future Food Fund & Portfolia Funds Trusted by Costco , Walmart , Whole Foods , Kroger & Albertsons What we do One company, the whole food supply chain Everything GrubMarket offers, in one place — no more hunting through separate sites. Most popular B2B eCommerce Access high quality, exclusive products at low prices, across the U.S. and Canada Buy Wholesale ERP Software Explore AI-powered solutions for inventory, warehouse, eCommerce, and more Learn more Enterprise AI Discover our revolutionary en"}, {"u": "investors.html", "t": "Investor Relations", "d": "GrubMarket investor relations: revenue, valuation, Series H funding, financial highlights, and SEC filings.", "b": "Home › Company › Investor Relations Investor Relations GrubMarket is the largest private food technology company in the U.S. — profitable, fast-growing, and consolidating a fragmented, multi-trillion-dollar industry through eCommerce, software, and AI. Latest results Investor contact Preview An illustrative look at GrubMarket's future investor relations hub. Events, figures, filings, and documents shown here are sample placeholders — not official disclosures. Sample data AMRKT not listed $24.80 ▲ +0.62 (+2.56%) Day range 24.10 – 25.05 GrubMarket is privately held — these are not real quotes View financials → Financials Stock info Analyst coverage Strategy Results & filings Presentations Reports Events FAQ Contact Financial dashboard Key metrics at a glance $2.4B Annual revenue 3 yrs Profitable (EBITDA) $4.5B Last valuation ~$600M Total raised $1.2B FY22 $1.5B FY23 $1.8B FY24 $2.1B FY25 $2.4B FY26 Annual revenue, FY2022–FY2026 (illustrative) Stock information Share price & trading data GrubMarket is privately held, so there is no publicly traded stock today. The figures below are illustrative — they show what this page will report once shares are listed. Ticker AMRKT Exchange NYSE Last price $24.80 Change ▲ +0.62 (+2.56%) Day range $24.10 – $25.05 52-week range $18.40 – $26.75 Market cap $4.5B Shares outstanding 181.5M Avg. daily volume 1.24M Fiscal year end December 31 Illustrative pre-IPO figures for this redesign — not quotes, guidance, or an offer to sell securities. Real-"}, {"u": "leadership.html", "t": "Leadership Team", "d": "Meet GrubMarket's leadership team building the technology transforming the American food supply chain.", "b": "Home › Company › Leadership Leadership team The people building the technology that's digitally transforming the American food supply chain. Leadership Meet the team MX Mike Xu Founder & CEO Founded GrubMarket in 2014 with a mission to digitally transform the food supply chain through eCommerce, software, and AI. GW Genevieve Wang Chief Software Product Officer Leads product for GrubMarket's software ecosystem — WholesaleWare, AI Orders, GrubAssist, and Orders IO. JD Jorge deNeve Chief Legal Officer Appointed December 2025 to lead legal, compliance, and corporate affairs as GrubMarket's acquisition pace and regulatory footprint grow across North America. Executive profiles reflect publicly announced roles; a full leadership directory will follow. A team built by acquisition and by design Genevieve Wang's team shipped the Spring 2026 software release across WholesaleWare, Orders IO, and AI Orders, and followed it with the Sales AI Agent — a pattern that repeats across GrubMarket's leadership: ship a capability, then use it internally before rolling it out network-wide. Much of the executive bench arrived the same way GrubMarket's products did — through acquisition, with founders and operators from companies like Coast Citrus Distributors and Schoenmann Produce staying on to run the businesses they built, now with GrubMarket's software and balance sheet behind them. By integrating our platform with our existing technology stack and AI development capabilities, we are uniquely p"}, {"u": "orders-io.html", "t": "Orders IO", "d": "Orders IO gives your business a custom-branded mobile ordering app, so customers order, browse deals, and check status anytime.", "b": "Home › Tech › Orders IO Orders IO Custom-branded mobile ordering apps that let your customers buy from you anytime, from anywhere. Request a demo B2B eCommerce Your storefront, in your customers' pocket Orders IO gives restaurants, retailers, and foodservice buyers a fast, self-service way to order from you — branded with your logo, colors, and catalog. Live order guides Customers browse their personalized order guide with up-to-date products and pricing. Reorder in seconds Order history and one-tap reordering make repeat purchases effortless. Notes & messaging Buyers leave notes and reach your team by phone, email, or chat without leaving the app. iOS & Android Native mobile apps, published under your brand, for ordering around the clock. Connected Integrated with the software you already run Orders IO plugs into leading food-distribution ERPs so orders flow straight into your system. WholesaleWare GrubMarket's produce ERP and eCommerce backbone. Thyme & Granite State Cloud ERPs for produce wholesalers and distributors. Frantoni & Produce Pro Regional and enterprise produce platforms. One app, built around your catalog Orders IO isn't a generic ordering app with your logo pasted on — it's generated from your live product catalog, pricing, and customer list, so what a buyer sees matches exactly what you sell. Distributors running WholesaleWare, Thyme Software, Granite State Software, Frantoni, or Produce Pro can turn it on without re-entering a single item, because Orders IO "}, {"u": "privacy.html", "t": "Privacy Policy", "d": "GrubMarket's privacy policy: how we collect, use, disclose, transfer, and store your information across our marketplace and services.", "b": "Home › Privacy Policy Privacy Policy How GrubMarket collects, uses, discloses, transfers, and stores your information. The GrubMarket Team wants you to be very comfortable using our Services, including trusting us with securing your information. As such we've developed this Privacy Policy that describes how we collect, use, disclose, transfer, and store your information. This Privacy Policy, incorporated by reference into the Terms of Use, governs your use of the Services. Please review this Privacy Policy carefully. Your use of any of the Services indicates that you have read, accepted and agreed to GrubMarket's privacy practices, as outlined in this Privacy Policy, and any other applicable terms. As used herein, the term \"personal information\" means information that can be associated with a specific person and could be used to identify that person. We do not consider personal information to include information that has been made anonymous or aggregated so that it can no longer be used, whether in combination with other information or otherwise, to identify a specific person. We may update this Privacy Policy at any time by posting the updated version on this site. It is your responsibility to review this Privacy Policy periodically for changes. Your continued use of any of the Services following the posting of the updated version will mean that you accept and agree to the updated Privacy Policy. Information Collected or Received We require a user to provide a valid email ad"}, {"u": "recognition.html", "t": "Recognition", "d": "GrubMarket's recognition, including TIME100, CNBC Disruptor 50, and sustainability awards for transforming the food supply chain.", "b": "Home › Company › Recognition Recognition Where GrubMarket's growth, innovation, and impact across the food supply chain have been recognized — judged on changing how the industry operates, not just on revenue. TIME100 Companies Industry Leaders · 2026 Named to TIME's inaugural list, judged on impact, innovation, ambition, and success. Read more → CNBC Disruptor 50 2023–2025 · No. 20 in 2025 Three consecutive years among the most innovative private companies in the U.S. Sustainability in the Food Industry The Shelby Report · 2025 For the Sustainable California initiative. Our sustainability work → Inventory Management Solution Provider of the Year 2025 For AI-powered inventory tools that automate distributor workflows. Explore Enterprise AI → See what's next Follow our latest milestones and announcements in the news. In the News Investor relations"}, {"u": "sec-filing-10k.html", "t": "Hypothetical Form 10-K", "d": "A hypothetical Form 10-K prepared for GrubMarket's investor relations redesign prototype.", "b": "Home › Investor Relations › SEC Filings › Form 10-K Hypothetical Annual Report — Form 10-K A mock, illustrative example of the annual report GrubMarket would file with the SEC as a public company — built for this site prototype, not a real filing. Hypothetical This document is entirely illustrative. GrubMarket is privately held and has not filed a Form 10-K with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. Nothing here is a real disclosure, offer, or solicitation — figures are drawn from this site's own sample financials for demonstration purposes only. Registrant GrubMarket, Inc. Form type 10-K (Illustrative) Fiscal year end December 31, 2025 State of incorporation Delaware Commission file no. 000-00000 (sample) Principal office San Francisco, CA Item 1 — Business Part I Item 1A — Risk Factors Part I Item 2 — Properties Part I Item 7 — Management's Discussion & Analysis Part II Item 8 — Financial Statements Part II Item 10 — Directors, Officers & Governance Part III Signatures Item 1 — Business GrubMarket, Inc. (\"GrubMarket,\" \"the Company,\" \"we,\" or \"our\") was founded in 2014 and operates a technology-enabled food supply chain platform spanning three integrated segments: a business-to-business wholesale marketplace, cloud-based enterprise software (including our WholesaleWare ERP, GrubAssist enterprise AI suite, Orders IO mobile commerce, and GrubPay payments products), and direct-to-consumer grocery delivery operated through a family of regional food-hub brands. The Company"}, {"u": "sec-filings.html", "t": "SEC Filings", "d": "GrubMarket SEC filings: access annual reports, quarterly results, and other regulatory documents.", "b": "Home › Investor Relations › SEC Filings SEC filings Search and filter GrubMarket, Inc.'s regulatory filings by form type, year, or keyword. Hypothetical GrubMarket is currently privately held and does not file with the SEC. The filings table below is an illustrative mock-up of what this page would look like following a future public offering — dates, form types, and documents are samples, not real disclosures. Filing history All filings Form type All form types 10-K — Annual report 10-Q — Quarterly report 8-K — Current report DEF 14A — Proxy statement S-1 — Registration statement Form 4 — Insider ownership Year All years 2026 2025 Keyword Reset filters Date Form Description Links Mar 2, 2026 10-K Annual Report Fiscal year ended December 31, 2025 View filing PDF May 5, 2026 10-Q Quarterly Report For the quarter ended March 31, 2026 View filing PDF Feb 3, 2026 8-K Current Report Item 3.02 — $50M Series H financing at ~$4.5B pre-money valuation View filing PDF Mar 16, 2026 DEF 14A Proxy Statement Notice of annual meeting of stockholders View filing PDF Nov 4, 2025 10-Q Quarterly Report For the quarter ended September 30, 2025 View filing PDF Nov 17, 2025 8-K Current Report Item 2.01 — Completion of acquisition of Procurant View filing PDF Aug 5, 2025 10-Q Quarterly Report For the quarter ended June 30, 2025 View filing PDF Jun 27, 2025 8-K Current Report Item 2.01 — Completion of acquisition of Coast Citrus Distributors View filing PDF Mar 10, 2025 S-1 Registration Statement Ini"}, {"u": "software.html", "t": "ERP Software", "d": "WholesaleWare is GrubMarket's cloud, AI-powered ERP for the fresh food supply chain: inventory, warehouse, accounting, and payments.", "b": "Home › Tech › ERP Software AI-powered software fueling digital transformation Improve efficiency, business insight, and customer satisfaction with GrubMarket's suite of software solutions built for the food supply chain. Explore modules See Enterprise AI Meet WholesaleWare® Run your whole operation on one platform WholesaleWare® is GrubMarket's cloud, AI-powered ERP for the fresh-food supply chain — covering inventory, warehouse management, grower accounting, HR, payments, and branded mobile ordering apps for wholesalers, distributors, and brokers, plus CSA management for farmers. Real-time inventory & warehouse visibility Grower accounting & payments built in Branded eCommerce & custom mobile apps Get started Modules Everything the food supply chain needs WholesaleWare® Cloud, AI-powered ERP for inventory, warehouse, grower accounting, and HR — the food industry's fastest-growing platform. GrubPay & Orders IO Accept ACH and card payments, and sell through your own branded mobile ordering apps. Farmigo® CSA and food-hub management built for farmers and local wholesalers. Built for perishables, not retrofitted from retail Generic retail ERPs treat produce like packaged goods with fixed SKUs and shelf lives. WholesaleWare was built from day one for the fresh food supply chain, where a case of tomatoes can shrink, ripen, or grade down before it ships. That means lot tracking, catch-weight billing, and grower settlements are core features, not add-ons — which is why GrubMarket ca"}, {"u": "sustainability.html", "t": "Sustainability", "d": "GrubMarket's Sustainable California initiative supports growers, reduces waste, and reinvigorates the state's agriculture.", "b": "Home › News › Sustainability Sustainability at GrubMarket Sustainable California demonstrates our commitment to preserving California's farming environment, empowering farmers, and reinvigorating the state's agricultural ecosystem. Learn about the initiative Shop fresh Sustainable California Protecting a fragile agricultural ecosystem We're committed to preserving the sustainability of California's farming environment — empowering farmers, reducing waste across the supply chain, and reinvigorating the agricultural ecosystem that feeds the nation. Empowering local farmers & growers Reducing food waste across the chain Reinvigorating California's ag ecosystem Get involved What Sustainable California has done so far Active since 2023, the initiative has sponsored the planting of more than 230,000 trees in at-risk regions across the state, including a 2025 partnership with One Tree Planted that put over 100,000 trees in the ground in the Sierra Nevada region alone. It has also given California farmers free access to GrubMarket's AI software, and partnered with CCOF (California Certified Organic Farmers) to sponsor ten disadvantaged farmers completing organic certification — a process that's normally too costly and time-consuming for many small growers to pursue on their own. The work was recognized in 2025 with The Shelby Report's Sustainability in the Food Industry award, but the initiative's real measure is upstream: fewer at-risk acres lost, and more small farms able to reach "}, {"u": "terms.html", "t": "Terms of Use", "d": "GrubMarket's Terms of Use governing your use of GrubMarket.com, its marketplace, software, and services.", "b": "Home › Terms of Use Terms of Use Welcome to GrubMarket.com! Please review these terms carefully before using the Services. GrubMarket, Inc. and/or its affiliates (\"GrubMarket\") make available to you this website, software, and other information, products and services when you visit GrubMarket.com, including associated sites linked thereto by GrubMarket (collectively, \"Site\"), use GrubMarket products and services, or use software provided by GrubMarket in connection with any of the foregoing (collectively, \"Services\"). By accessing or otherwise using the Services in any way, you agree to and are bound by the Terms of Use of GrubMarket, including the GrubMarket Privacy Policy and all other GrubMarket policies posted on the Site (collectively, \"Terms of Use\" or \"Agreement\"). Please carefully review the GrubMarket Terms of Use by clicking the \"Terms\" link near the bottom of the Home Page of GrubMarket.com, or directly via its URL (i.e., web address) at www.grubmarket.com/terms using your personal computer, smartphone, or other electronic devices. GrubMarket reserves the right, at its sole discretion, to change, modify, add or remove portion of these Terms of Use at any time. The updated version of Terms of Use will be posted at the Site. It is your responsibility to review these Terms of Use periodically for changes. Your continued use of the Services following the posting of changes will mean that you accept and agree to the updated version. GrubMarket is an online marketplace f"}, {"u": "trade-shows.html", "t": "Trade Shows", "d": "Meet GrubMarket on the floor and see WholesaleWare, AI Orders, and Orders IO live at produce and food-technology events.", "b": "Home › News › Trade Shows Trade shows Where to meet the GrubMarket team on the floor — see our software live and talk through your operation. Where we go Meet us across the industry We exhibit and speak at leading produce, foodservice, and food-technology events across North America. Produce & foodservice expos See WholesaleWare, AI Orders, and Orders IO demonstrated live for distributors and wholesalers. Food technology conferences Hear how enterprise AI is transforming procurement, inventory, and the fresh food supply chain. Grower & ag events Learn how growers reach more buyers and get paid faster through the GrubMarket network. Sample categories for this redesign — a live schedule of upcoming shows will be published here. What you'll actually see on the floor Rather than a generic product pitch, GrubMarket's booth teams typically run live demos against real scenarios: an AI Orders agent parsing an actual customer email into a structured order in real time, or a Sales AI Agent building a price sheet from a photographed menu on the spot. It's a deliberate choice — distributors have seen enough vaporware demos to be skeptical, so the team would rather show software working against messy, real-world inputs than a polished slide. Want to connect at a show? Reach out to schedule a meeting or request a live demo. Contact the team See all events"}, {"u": "wholesale.html", "t": "Buy Wholesale", "d": "Buy wholesale through GrubMarket's B2B network. Source thousands of products at exclusive, low prices across the U.S. and Canada.", "b": "Home › Buy & Sell › Buy Wholesale Wholesale food buying, reimagined Tap into GrubMarket's unparalleled B2B network and source thousands of high-quality products at exclusive, low prices — across the U.S. and Canada. Start buying Find a wholesaler near you Why GrubMarket An unparalleled network for buying wholesale Serving all of the U.S. and Canada, GrubMarket's extensive and growing network of wholesalers and distributors sells across every segment — from grocers to foodservice to schools, government, local markets, and restaurants. Thousands of exclusive products at low prices Coast-to-coast distribution & logistics Quality produce, year after year Buy Wholesale Who we serve Built for every corner of foodservice Grocers & markets Keep shelves stocked with fresh, competitively priced inventory delivered on your schedule. Restaurants & foodservice Source consistent, high-quality ingredients with reliable fulfillment you can plan around. Schools & government Meet volume and compliance needs with a vetted, nationwide supplier network. A network built through acquisition, not just growth GrubMarket's wholesale network is the product of more than 70 acquisitions — regional distributors like Coast Citrus Distributors, the largest acquisition in company history and a major U.S. supplier of tropical produce, and century-old operators like Schoenmann Produce, serving the Gulf Coast since 1910. Each joins the same WholesaleWare backbone rather than staying siloed, which is why a singl"}];
